{"id": "EUVD-2026-101043", "enisaUuid": "0ea3f1a5-f6d5-39d2-aab3-c8a44f2844c1", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\naf_unix: Return immediately when manage_oob() returns NULL for 0-length buffer.\n\nFahad Alharbi reported that recv(0, MSG_PEEK) triggers busy-wait\nin unix_stream_read_generic() if recv() is blocking and the last\nskb in the queue is MSG_OOB skb.\n\nIn such a situation, TCP returns 0 immediately regardless of\nblocking or non-blocking.\n\nLet's follow the behaviour.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T13:25:57", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:18:47", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3d3c7a3df66b2ca3d2cd1a2a0c37eb701feba713", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d5dd55b316ca229a4cbf11729483ba5bb57233e7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c81c5be3826c8467945b964d0cf7f7b3d65461db", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6e5ee08eb5858d175da6768d75d163817b6a9d4a"], "aliases": ["GHSA-78rw-466c-3p7p", "CVE-2026-98394"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0bb37237-6cfe-35e2-ace7-f44b3e64749a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "314001f0bf927015e459c9d387d62a231fe93af3 <3d3c7a3df66b2ca3d2cd1a2a0c37eb701feba713"}, {"id": "1cfa43c0-4147-311c-8b8a-bdea891f68c6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "1fd742b1-1ddc-3ee4-9f53-d8b1b6be095e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15"}, {"id": "3543a7a7-8b5d-3f32-b856-1f5f1a6fb1f1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "314001f0bf927015e459c9d387d62a231fe93af3 <6e5ee08eb5858d175da6768d75d163817b6a9d4a"}, {"id": "9e0773a1-5e95-335a-87e9-6a00eb942626", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "314001f0bf927015e459c9d387d62a231fe93af3 <c81c5be3826c8467945b964d0cf7f7b3d65461db"}, {"id": "adafcafa-c51c-374a-